For any real number r, the Maclaurin series for \(f(x)=(1+x)^r\) is the binomial series. It converges to f for \(|x|\lt 1\), and we write
  \[(1+x)^r=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\binom{r}{n}x^n\]\[=1+rx+\frac{r(r-1)}{2!}x^2+\cdots+\frac{r(r-1)\cdots(r-n+1)}{n!}x^n+\cdots\]
  for \(|x|\lt 1\)
